        "decision_notes": "Gate 6A audited this Downstream capital deployment authority record. The Atlas intent is a posture hard-invariants surface with block_active, hard_block_reasons, and zero_deployable_required. Native posture contracts carry permission_state, local_envelope, hard_invariants, and reasons, and Tier B boundary proof keeps posture output separate from capital deployment decision fields. Native capital deployment surfaces provide stand_down and zero authorised_notional_usd when final_risk_action is not proceed, but they do not own or expose the typed posture hard-invariants fields. The useful native expression therefore requires owner/surface transformation rather than treating the current capital-deployment target as satisfied. Gate 7 proof resolution remains staged.\nGate 7A proof resolution: Tier B proof posture; test-family action admit_new; existing-test decision new_test_family_required; proof-block action admit_new; checkpoint declaration required false; docstring declaration required true; implementation leaf later_blueprint_leaf. Governing proof surfaces are cited in native_evidence."
